{#
  Shared "book a meeting" button. One markup source for every place this
  button appears (hero, last action section, footer, case study pages),
  per Christopher's direct request. Always opens Calendly's real popup
  scheduler; never links to an anchor. Pass riskReversal=true for the
  case study pages' third disclaimer line. Pass showPhone=false to omit
  the "or call or text at" line, used once (the homepage's final
  booking section) on direct request, since the number already
  appears earlier on that same page. The "or email directly" mailto
  line, added on a September 2026 build instruction, always shows
  regardless of showPhone: unlike the phone number, the email address
  isn't shown anywhere earlier on the homepage by the time you reach
  that section.
  Button text is "Schedule your call today," changed from "Schedule a
  call with me" (itself changed from "Book a call with me," itself
  changed from "Book a free strategy call," itself changed from "Book
  my meeting with you," itself changed from the original "Book my 15
  minute call") on direct request, via a Vercel toolbar comment on the
  hero CTA reading "Schedule your call today (apply to all ctas)."
#}
{% macro button(wrapClass="actions", riskReversal=false, showPhone=true) %}
<div class="{{ wrapClass }}">
  <a class="cta" href="https://calendly.com/aweb3dad/15-minute-greeting" onclick="Calendly.initPopupWidget({url:'https://calendly.com/aweb3dad/15-minute-greeting'});return false;">
    <span>Schedule your call today</span>
  </a>
  {% if showPhone %}<p class="call-alt">or call or text at <a href="tel:+13107036003">(310) 703-6003</a></p>{% endif %}
  <p class="call-alt">or <a href="mailto:christopher@theweb3family.com?subject=Booking%20a%20call">email directly</a></p>
  {% if riskReversal %}<p class="risk-reversal">Try it out today. Month to month. Everything built is yours.</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endmacro %}
